Description: traffic accounting and quota rate limits for Proxmox VE virtual machines
 Counts the traffic of each network device of QEMU virtual machines since its
 last reset. When the counted traffic reaches the quota of the device, its
 rate in the VM configuration is set to a configurable limit rate; a reset
 restores the original rate.
 .
 Counters and settings are kept cluster-wide per VMID and network device: they
 survive the VM being destroyed and re-created (reinstall), follow migrations,
 and include the traffic up to the very end when a VM or the host shuts down.
 .
 Adds a Traffic page to the Datacenter and VM views of the web interface and
 the /cluster/trafficd API, e.g. for billing systems doing the periodic reset.
